.TH AXON 1 "2026-10-11" "Axon" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
axon \- query installed packages and cached Arch repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-Q
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-Qi
.IR PACKAGE ...
.PP
.B axon
.RB [ \-\-config " PATH" ]
.B \-Ss
.IR PATTERN ...
.PP
.B axon \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
Axon is a C frontend to libalpm for the NeurOS distribution project.
The current command-line interface lists installed packages, displays
installed-package metadata, and searches locally cached repository databases.
It does not install, remove, upgrade, or download packages, or refresh repositories.
.PP
Select exactly one operation:
.B \-Q
or
.BR \-S .
The information and search flags modify those operations; they are not
standalone commands.
Output is written to standard output and diagnostics to standard error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-Q ", " \-\-query
List installed package names and versions, one package per line.
Without
.BR \-i ,
this operation takes no package arguments.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-info
With
.BR \-Q ,
show the name, version, description, architecture, URL, installed size in bytes,
and installation reason for each named installed package.
At least one exact package name is required.
Missing packages are reported as errors; remaining names are still processed.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sync
Select repository queries.
Currently requires
.BR \-s .
This flag does not synchronize or update databases.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-search
With
.BR \-S ,
search cached repository data using libalpm regular expressions.
At least one pattern is required, and all patterns must match.
Matching packages are printed as repository/name and version, followed by
the description.
The same package may appear in multiple repositories.
No matches produces empty output and a successful exit status.
Missing or unreadable database caches produce an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /etc/pacman.conf .
The form
.BI \-\-config= PATH
is also accepted.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display usage and exit without loading configuration.
The process identity check still applies.
.TP
.B \-\-
End option processing.
Use this before a package name or pattern beginning with a dash.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Axon reads pacman-style options and repository sections, including
Include directives, mirror substitutions, and signature policies.
Relative Include paths are resolved against the process working directory.
.PP
The reader rejects unknown directives, invalid values, duplicate repositories,
missing includes, include cycles, and configured resource-limit violations.
It is intentionally stricter than pacman for some malformed configurations.
Comments must occupy a whole line; an inline hash character is retained.
.PP
XferCommand is parsed but is not supported by backend setup.
A configuration containing it causes an explicit error, including for queries.
Frontend settings such as Color are retained but are not implemented by this
basic interface.
.PP
Query commands do not begin transactions or refresh databases.
Backend initialization follows libalpm's filesystem behavior and may create
database directories where permitted.
.SS Downloads and verification
The shared backend uses the configured Server order for mirror fallback and
honors CacheDir, ParallelDownloads, DownloadUser, CheckSpace, and signature
settings.  DownloadUser must name an existing account; an unknown account is
an error.  Axon does not silently select another account or disable the sandbox.
DisableSandbox, DisableSandboxFilesystem, and DisableSandboxSyscalls are
explicit configuration overrides.
.PP
SigLevel, LocalFileSigLevel, and RemoteFileSigLevel control verification.
Required signatures must be present and valid under the configured trust policy
and GPGDir keyring.  Verification failures do not cause an unsigned retry.
.PP
The backend refresh-and-upgrade workflow requires a successful repository
refresh before preparing a full system upgrade for approval.
A failed refresh can leave some cached databases updated; it does not authorize
package installation from that partial refresh.
Cancellation is cooperative: a transfer or package operation already underway
may finish before interruption takes effect.  Completed changes are not rolled
back automatically.  Cleanup failures are reported separately from the original
operation failure, and Axon does not blindly remove an existing database lock.
.PP
These backend workflows are not yet exposed as command-line operations.
The query commands described above continue to use cached data without downloads.
.SH PRIVILEGES
These query operations do not require root, but the configuration and databases
must be accessible to the invoking user.
Axon does not request passwords or automatically elevate privileges.
.PP
Setuid/setgid-style execution, mismatched real/effective/saved identities,
and secure-execution launches are rejected.
Install Axon as a normal executable without setuid/setgid bits or file capabilities.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The operation completed successfully, including a search with no matches.
.TP
.B 1
A configuration, privilege, backend, or output error occurred, or a requested
installed package was not found.
.TP
.B 2
An option, operation combination, or required argument was invalid.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/pacman.conf
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/local/
Default installed-package database.
.TP
.I /var/lib/pacman/sync/
Default cached repository databases.
.PP
RootDir and DBPath configuration can change the database locations.
.SH EXAMPLES
List installed packages:
.PP
.nf
    axon \-Q
.fi
.PP
Inspect two installed packages:
.PP
.nf
    axon \-Qi pacman glibc
.fi
.PP
Use the equivalent long options:
.PP
.nf
    axon \-\-query \-\-info pacman
.fi
.PP
Search cached repositories, quoting the pattern to prevent shell expansion:
.PP
.nf
    axon \-Ss '^pacman$'
.fi
.PP
Use an alternate configuration:
.PP
.nf
    axon \-\-config /path/to/pacman.conf \-Q
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR pacman.conf (5),
.BR libalpm (3)
